Here are the four TUnit lifecycle scopes with the attributes and where they go:

---

### 1. Before every test in a class — `[Before(Test)]` / `[After(Test)]`

```csharp
public class OrderTests
{
    [Before(Test)]
    public async Task ResetDatabase(TestContext context)
    {
        await InMemoryDb.ResetAsync();
    }

    [After(Test)]
    public async Task Cleanup(TestContext context)
    {
        // optional per-test teardown
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task Order_IsCreated() { /* ... */ }
}
```

You can also use a **constructor** or `IAsyncDisposable.DisposeAsync` instead.

---

### 2. Once per class — `[Before(Class)]` / `[After(Class)]`

```csharp
public class CustomerServiceTests
{
    private static ServiceFixture _fixture = null!;

    [Before(Class)]
    public static async Task OpenFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        _fixture = await ServiceFixture.CreateAsync();
    }

    [After(Class)]
    public static async Task DisposeFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        await _fixture.DisposeAsync();
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task Can_Create_Customer() { /* use _fixture */ }
}
```

> These methods must be **static**.

---

### 3. Once per assembly — `[Before(Assembly)]` / `[After(Assembly)]`

```csharp
public class WireMockHook
{
    [Before(Assembly)]
    public static async Task StartServer(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        await WireMockServer.StartAsync();
    }

    [After(Assembly)]
    public static async Task StopServer(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        await WireMockServer.StopAsync();
    }
}
```

The class can live anywhere in the assembly — TUnit discovers it automatically.

---

### 4. Once per entire test session — `[Before(TestSession)]` / `[After(TestSession)]`

```csharp
public class GlobalSetup
{
    [Before(TestSession)]
    public static async Task Migrate(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        await EfCoreMigrator.ApplyMigrationsAsync();
    }

    [After(TestSession)]
    public static async Task TearDown(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        await EfCoreMigrator.DropDatabaseAsync();
    }
}
```

Runs once across all assemblies in the test run.

---

### Quick-reference summary

| Scope | Before | After | Method must be | Context type |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Each test | `[Before(Test)]` | `[After(Test)]` | instance | `TestContext` |
| Class | `[Before(Class)]` | `[After(Class)]` | **static** | `ClassHookContext` |
| Assembly | `[Before(Assembly)]` | `[After(Assembly)]` | **static** | `AssemblyHookContext` |
| Session | `[Before(TestSession)]` | `[After(TestSession)]` | **static** | `TestSessionContext` |

**Bonus:** `[BeforeEvery(Test)]` / `[AfterEvery(Test)]` (and `Class`/`Assembly` variants) are cross-cutting — they fire for *every* test/class/assembly in the run, useful for global logging or diagnostics. The context parameter and `CancellationToken` are optional on all hooks.
